      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "U# is still compiling automatically, and its 02.02.2026...\n\n3.10.1 SDK World+Base, Unity 2022.3.22f1.\n\nPlease guys, fix this already. I am heavily coding with multiple C#>U# Codes and getting the compiler to freeze Unity is not pleasant. It is either stopping a habit of pushing ctrl+s non stop (which is not going to work) or making a function, which is toggleable, working properly.",
